{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788351032,"nonce":"b9TqKFdvsyx2oyIfteUn7Kzi1jc=","message":"**Root cause settled by investigation, orchestrator, repair round 2026-09-02.** The issue records that \"which of those it is has NOT been investigated\" and offers two candidates. Read against `Verse/Room.cs` `Owners` by member name — neither is right as stated:\n\n```csharp\npublic IEnumerable\u003cPawn\u003e Owners {\n  get {\n    if (TouchesMapEdge || IsHuge || (Role != RoomRoleDefOf.Bedroom \u0026\u0026 Role != RoomRoleDefOf.PrisonCell\n        \u0026\u0026 Role != RoomRoleDefOf.Barracks \u0026\u0026 Role != RoomRoleDefOf.PrisonBarracks)) yield break;\n    IEnumerable\u003cBuilding_Bed\u003e enumerable = ContainedBeds.Where(x =\u003e x.def.building.bed_humanlike);\n    if (enumerable.Count() \u003e 1 \u0026\u0026 (Role == RoomRoleDefOf.Barracks || Role == RoomRoleDefOf.PrisonBarracks)\n        \u0026\u0026 enumerable.Where(b =\u003e b.OwnersForReading.Any()).Count() \u003e 1) yield break;\n    foreach (Building_Bed item in enumerable) { ... yield return assignedPawns[i]; }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nRoom 38 is a Barracks with three humanlike beds, three of them owned, so it hits the **second** `yield break` exactly. `owners_total: 0` is vanilla's own semantics. Nothing threw; the bare `catch {}` never fired.\n\n**Candidate 1 was right in substance and wrong in the detail that decides the fix.** The gate is not the Barracks role — it is *more than one owned bed*. A Barracks with exactly one owned bed yields that owner normally, which is why this never surfaced until a third colonist claimed a bed.\n\nThree consequences that bind the fix:\n\n1. **The rollup must come from `ContainedBeds` / `OwnersForReading`** — the same route the `beds[]` block at `PlaceVerbs.cs:173-192` already uses and gets right. `room.Owners` is the wrong source for \"who sleeps here\" and cannot be repaired by catching harder. Acceptance item 2's first branch (\"derived from the same per-bed data\") is therefore the correct one, and the `Journal.EmitWarning` alternative would have been papering over a semantic mismatch.\n2. **`TouchesMapEdge` and `IsHuge` are two further silent-empty conditions** nobody had accounted for. A barracks touching the map edge reports no owners for a third distinct reason, and acceptance item 3's list of genuinely-0 cases should grow to cover it.\n3. **The bare `catch {}` is a real latent hazard and is not this bug.** Replacing it with one that records that it fired still stands per acceptance item 2, but doing that alone would have changed nothing while looking like a fix.\n\nVanilla's `Owners` is not broken — it answers \"whose room is this\", while the mod was asking \"who sleeps in here\". The two agree on every room with fewer than two owned beds.\n\nRecorded in DESIGN.md's decisions log (commit c901f5b) so it lands in a diff rather than only in a comment.","files":null}]}